    "title": "Mobile woman sentenced to prison for trafficking fentanyl - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Michael Hanich ,\n1 hours ago\nVideo above: ‘News 5 Now’ — Top Stories from Sept. 16, 2026\nMOBILE COUNTY. Ala. (WKRG) – A Mobile woman has been sentenced to serve time in person for trafficking fentanyl.\nArgument over missing dog ends in deadly baseball bat attack in Thomasville According to a news release from the U.S. Department of Justice’s Southern District of Alabama, Amada Guy, 46, of Mobile, was sentenced to 84 months in prison.\nThis case stems from an incident on Oct. 5, 2022, when the Mobile County Sheriff’s Office and Alabama Law Enforcement Agency had an undercover informant purchase 15.06 grams of fentanyl from Guy. On Oct. 13, deputies seized 18.08 grams of pure methamphetamine from Guy’s vehicle.\nThe release said deputies executed a search warrant for Guy at a Mobile home on Jan. 26, 2023. During the search, deputies found small amounts of methamphetamine, fentanyl and two digital scales.\nDaphne police search for missing juvenile last seen in Lake Forest MCSO, ALEA and the Bureau of Alcohol, Tobacco, Firearms, and Explosives investigated this case.\nCopyright 2026 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed.\nFor the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to WKRG News 5.",
    "summary": "Ala. (WKRG) – A Mobile woman has been sentenced to serve time in person for trafficking fentanyl. Argument over missing dog ends in deadly baseball bat attack in Thomasville According to a news release from the U.S. Department of Justice’s Southern District of Alabama, Amada Guy, 46, of Mobile, was sentenced to 84 months in prison. This case stems from an incident on Oct. 5, 2022, when the Mobile County Sheriff’s Office and Alabama Law Enforcement Agency had an undercover informant purchase 15.06 grams of fentanyl from Guy.",
